    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "Across the political spectrum German outlets converge on the view that the energy transition is already generating sharp electricity and heating price spikes that threaten household budgets and industrial competitiveness. They also uniformly stress that without a rapid expansion of transmission infrastructure such as Suedlink and sufficient storage capacity, the planned phase‑out of coal and nuclear will jeopardise supply security. Consequently, most commentators, from left‑liberal to conservative‑liberal, call for a pragmatic interim energy mix that retains some nuclear or gas capacity while scaling renewables, rather than an abrupt abandonment of all baseload sources.",
      "controversial_points": "The core conflict pits nuclear phase‑out advocates against proponents of nuclear as a bridge to climate targets."
